 "text": "Sound: a lo-fi, digital, video-game-gone-wrong lead: a square wave reduced to a few bits, with whining aliases following every note.\n\nHow it's built: a pulse wave straight into the Crusher at 5 bits and a quarter of the sample rate, then a filter to take the harshest edge off, a short envelope and a Delay. Two voices.\n\nPlay: quick melodies, arpeggios; high notes whine more.\n\nTweak: BITS and RATE, WIDTH, the filter's CUTOFF.",
